+After simulating 100 USDT of Aave yield on a 1,000 USDT deposit, the depositor's underlying balance still reports 1,000 USDT instead of 1,100 USDT. When the depositor fully exits, 103 USDT worth of aUSDT remains in the vault: 100 USDT of yield plus the 3 USDT withdrawal fee.
+
+### Fix I would make
+
+Use the vault's real Aave position as the asset base, not a stale internal counter. `totalAssets()` should derive from `aUsdt.balanceOf(address(this))` plus any idle USDT held by the vault if idle assets are possible. Then base `convertToShares`, `convertToAssets`, and withdrawal accounting on that live asset value. Add tests that simulate aToken balance growth and verify that share price and `balanceOfUnderlying` increase.
